title: 'What I would build: receipts over a default.'
pid: de846cc7-205d-4275-8a44-65b07b9a5e10
body: |2-
  A node is new if it changed since the subscription's default baseline
  and has no receipt matching its present state. The default is set when
  the subscription is made, and moved forward when the reader says "all
  of this is processed"; receipts older than it can then be dropped. The
  default comes from 3 or 5; I lean to 5, for uncommitted work. The
  receipts are the same store Vic needs to remember which of another's
  changes were processed, and should be one store.
